WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.420
Speaker 1: Many of you have been emailing
me about the Pandora papers, and I want to

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:10.360
start and do sort of like a brief overview
of what the Pandora papers are and kind of

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.610
show you how I would go through learning about
what is here now.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:20.780
One completely reasonable way to start would
be go directly to the source material, which

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:21.780
we're going to do.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.800
I'm actually for this particular segment.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.020
I'm going to start with the Wiki article about
the Pandora papers.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.650
Now a lot of people will say, David, anybody
can edit Wikipedia.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.550
It's not actually a source.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.660
And Wikipedia would admit that Wikipedia,
you have to source the things that are there,

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.150
although there are inaccuracies in Wikipedia
in this particular article, I actually think

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:47.100
that it's a good place to start to get an
overview of what this is about.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.440
Then we go to primary sources, then we go
to articles about it.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.950
So what are the Pandora papers?

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:58.640
The Pandora papers are eleven point nine million
leaked documents that were published by the

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.580
ICJ, the International Consortium of Investigative
Journalists, starting on October 3rd.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:10.920
Two days ago, the leak exposed the secret
offshore accounts of 35 world leaders, including

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.030
current and former presidents, prime ministers
and heads of state, as well as more than 100

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.659
billionaires, celebrities and business leaders.

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:23.799
The news organizations of the ICJ described
the document leak as their most expansive

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:28.759
exposé of financial secrecy yet, containing
documents, images, emails and spreadsheets

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:33.719
from 14 financial service companies in nations
including Panama, Switzerland and the Arab

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:38.939
Emirates, surpassing their previous release
of the Panama Papers in 2016.

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:44.590
At the time of the release of the papers,
the ICJ said it is not identifying its source.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:50.259
Up to an estimated thirty two trillion U.S.
dollars, excluding non-monetary valuables

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:55.499
such as real estate, art and jewelry, may
be hidden from being taxed, according to news

00:01:55.499 --> 00:01:56.499
reports.

00:01:56.499 --> 00:01:58.020
Now just to hear.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:02.630
There are 12 different citations that we could
look at.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:07.770
OK, the next part is about disclosures.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:13.129
There is a sub article, a list of people named
in the Pandora papers, which you can look

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:14.150
at separately.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:19.879
It lists heads of state and it goes from the
king of Jordan Abdullah, the second through,

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:24.270
you know, the Chilean president, the Kenyan
president.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:32.290
It includes former heads of state as well
heads of government, including Patrick Achi,

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:36.520
the prime minister of Cote d'Ivoire, and many
others.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.519
Heads of organizations, ministers, bankers.

00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:46.000
Some of these individual names will be meaningful
to people, some less so royalty, including

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.260
the former King of Spain, Juan Carlos, business
people on and on and on.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.420
So we now have sort of like an initial understanding
of what this is.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:03.209
These are disclosures about the financial
holdings, assets and accounts of important

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:05.500
or elite individuals.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.599
Where do we go next?

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:11.400
Next, we go to the actual disclosures on the
website of the International Consortium of

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.400
Investigative Journalists.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:18.430
This is filled with various articles and different
documents.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:24.579
Many of these start to be sort of commentaries
on the Pandora papers, but one thing you can

00:03:24.579 --> 00:03:31.299
go to is the key findings section from the
organization that put this together itself.

00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:35.450
The key findings are and again, we're just
we're building our understanding of what this

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.450
is.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:41.390
An investigation by more than 600 journalists
from hundred and fifty news outlets has unearthed

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:47.440
offshore dealings of 35 current and former
world leaders and more than 300 other current

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.100
and former public officials and politicians.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:55.930
The offshore system continues to thrive despite
decades of legislation, investigations and

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:00.180
international agreements aimed at combating
money laundering and tax dodging.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.750
South Dakota and more than a dozen U.S. states
have become leaders in the business of selling

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:10.900
financial secrecy, even as the U.S. blames
smaller nations for enabling tax avoidance

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:11.900
and dirty money flows.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.969
That's important, you know, very often it's
believed that if you want to do tax avoidance

00:04:15.969 --> 00:04:20.810
and shield assets, you go to the Caribbean,
you go to Switzerland, et cetera.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:27.230
But actually, South Dakota and some other
states have become really nexuses or neck

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:30.690
ci in this apparatus.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:35.750
The Pandora papers unmask the hidden owners
of offshore companies secret bank accounts,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:40.790
private jets, yachts, mansions and artworks
by Picasso banks and other masters.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:46.980
The biggest lick of the biggest lick the biggest
leak in ICJ history contains almost three

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:51.350
terabytes of information from 14 offshore
service providers.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:56.410
So then you could go and look at the actual
data if you wanted.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:59.630
This is another part of the website, which
at this immediate moment.

